- IsolationVM's hook gets --write / in a writable workspace (LLD), so the file tools can also rewrite the scratch .factory-claude/ (the settings and hook a Repair restarts with). Accepted: in the VM the hook is a guard against mistakes, not a boundary (a Bash command could bypass it anyway); the VM and the gateway are the boundary.
- A VM run whose task has no resolved auth runs on the subscription (the PoC's mode): the VM has no owner's environment or login to tell the mode from. Not in the LLD; listed as a departure.
- A read-only VM workspace keeps the host's hook roots (out/, tmp/) and --disallowedTools.
